```
import requests
import json

url = "https://www.example.com/api/passwords"

data = {
    "username": "admin",
    "password": "password123"
}

headers = {
    "content-type": "application/json"
}

response = requests.post(url, data=json.dumps(data), headers=headers)

if response.status_code == 200:
    print("password collected successfully!")
else:
    print("error occurred while collecting password.")
```

this code uses the requests library to send a post request to the school administrator's password collection endpoint. The data to be sent includes the username and password of the administrator. The response is checked for a successful status code (200) to indicate that the password has been collected successfully. If the status code is not 200, an error message is printed.

